HOW TO EMBED SHANE'S BUTCHER APP (Jotform to Website)\
\
PART A: Get the Code from Jotform\
1. Open the Butcher Shop form in your Jotform account.\
2. Click the orange "PUBLISH" tab at the top center of the screen.\
3. On the left-side menu, click "Embed".\
4. Click the big green "Copy Code" button.\
\
PART B: Put it on Shane's Website\
1. Log into Shane's website editor (likely WordPress via SiteGround).\
2. Create a brand new page called "Order Online" or "Click-and-Collect".\
3. Add a "Custom HTML" block to the page editor.\
4. Paste the Jotform code you just copied directly into that HTML block.\
5. Hit "Publish" or "Update" on the page.\
6. Add the new "Order Online" page to his main website navigation menu. The app will automatically resize to fit mobile and desktop screens!\
\
HOW TO SET UP & EMBED SHANE'S BUTCHER APP (Jotform)\
\
--- PART 1: EMBEDDING ON HIS WEBSITE ---\
1. In Jotform, click the orange "PUBLISH" tab at the top.\
2. On the left menu, click "Embed" and click the green "Copy Code" button.\
3. Log into Shane's website editor (likely WordPress via SiteGround).\
4. Create a new page called "Order Online" or "Click-and-Collect".\
5. Add a "Custom HTML" block to the page and paste the Jotform code.\
6. Hit "Publish" and add the page to his main website menu.\
\
--- PART 2: THE SHOP APP (How Shane gets the orders) ---\
Instead of just checking email, Shane can use a tablet or phone at the butcher block.\
1. Have Shane download the free "Jotform Mobile Forms" app on his iPad or iPhone.\
2. Log in with the account credentials.\
3. Turn on "Push Notifications". \
4. Now, every time a customer orders, his iPad will "ding" like a cash register, and he can view the exact order details, customer name, and pickup time right on the screen.\
\
--- PART 3: STOCK TRACKING (Inventory Management) ---\
To make sure he doesn't oversell a package he ran out of:\
1. In the Jotform Builder, click on the Meat Packages list.\
2. Hover over a specific package (e.g., "The Ultimate Family BBQ Box") and click the Pencil icon (Edit).\
3. Click the "Stock" tab at the top of the right-side menu.\
4. Toggle "Enable Stock Control" to ON.\
5. Type in how many he has available (e.g., 10). \
6. Jotform will automatically count down as people buy them. When it hits 0, it will say "Sold Out" and prevent customers from ordering it!\
\
--- PART 4: ACCOUNT CONNECTION (Taking Payments) ---\
Right now it is set to "Pay at Pickup". If he wants customers to pay online with a credit card:\
1. In the Jotform Builder, click the "+" (Add Form Element) button on the left.\
2. Click the "Payments" tab.\
3. Click the three dots next to "Purchase Order" and select "Switch to another gateway".\
4. Choose his preferred processor (Square or Stripe are best).\
5. A menu will pop up on the right. Click the blue "Connect" button and have Shane log into his Square/Stripe account.\
6. Jotform handles all the security and PCI compliance automatically!\
